r":27,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now the daughters of Zelophehad son of Hepher, the son of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh, belonged to the clans of Manasseh son of Joseph. These were the names of his daughters: Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah. They approached","from":33},{"book":"JOS","chapter":17,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now this was the allotment for the tribe of Manasseh as Josephʼs firstborn son, namely for Machir the firstborn of Manasseh and father of the Gileadites, who had received Gilead and Bashan because Machir was a man of war.","from":29},{"book":"1CH","chapter":7,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The sons of Issachar: Tola, Puah, Jashub, and Shimron—four in all.","from":23},{"book":"GEN","chapter":30,"verse":17,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And God listened to Leah, and she conceived and bore a fifth son to Jacob. Then Leah said, “God has rewarded me for giving my maidservant to my husband.” So she named him Issachar.","from":23},{"book":"GEN","chapter":30,"verse":19,"verseEnd":20,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Again Leah conceived and bore a sixth son to Jacob. “God has given me a good gift,” she said. “This time my husband will honor me, because I have borne him six sons.” And she named him Zebulun.","from":26},{"book":"GEN","chapter":41,"verse":51,"verseEnd":52,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Joseph named the firstborn Manasseh, saying, “God has made me forget all my hardship and all my fatherʼs household.” And the second son he named Ephraim, saying, “God has made me fruitful in the land of my affliction.”","from":28},{"book":"GEN","chapter":46,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The sons of Issachar: Tola, Puvah, Job, and Shimron.","from":24}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"38-51":{"people":[{"id":"bela-h1106a","name":"Bela","kind":"person"