e":2,"uses":12},{"base":"H5070","lemma":"נָדָב","tr":"na·dav","gloss":"Nadab","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":20},{"base":"H0175","lemma":"אַהֲרֹן","tr":"a·ha·ron","gloss":"Aaron","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":347},{"base":"H6955","lemma":"קְהָת","tr":"qe·hat","gloss":"Kohath","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":32}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1CO","chapter":10,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"Nevertheless, God was not pleased with most of them, for they were struck down in the wilderness.","from":65},{"book":"1CO","chapter":10,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"These things took place as examples to keep us from craving evil things as they did.","from":65},{"book":"NUM","chapter":14,"verse":38,"verseEnd":38,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Of those men who had gone to spy out the land, only Joshua son of Nun and Caleb son of Jephunneh remained alive.","from":65},{"book":"EXO","chapter":6,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And Amram married his fatherʼs sister Jochebed, and she bore him Aaron and Moses. Amram lived 137 years.","from":59},{"book":"DEU","chapter":2,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"The time we spent traveling from Kadesh-barnea until we crossed over the Brook of Zered was thirty-eight years, until that entire generation of fighting men had perished from the camp, as the LORD had sworn to them.","from":64},{"book":"DEU","chapter":2,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Indeed, the LORDʼs hand was against them, to eliminate them from the camp, until they had all perished.","from":64},{"book":"GEN","chapter":46,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.","from":57},{"book":"EXO","chapter":2,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Now a man of the house of Levi married a Levite woman,","from":59}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":11},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}